---
/**
 * Home `.process` — the "Vivid Smile Cosmetic Process" on charcoal: centred
 * head (hairline eyebrow, italic h2, the `.pcp` sub-line, a paragraph), the
 * white plate of three numbered steps, and the signature line — Dr. Bryce's
 * round avatar beside his name and "Creator · Vivid Smile Cosmetic Process".
 *
 * A code_section band, registered as `home_process` in
 * src/blocks/CodeSectionBlock.astro. The section has no id in the template
 * (index.astro:511 `<section class="process">`), so its BANDS entry sets
 * `anchorProp: null` and this component takes no `id` — adding one would be an
 * attribute-level delta on the live route.
 *
 * ── Why code and not process_steps (D5, 2026-09-08) ───────────────────────
 * ProcessStepsBlock's `card` shape is this plate element for element, but the
 * layout has no field for the `.pcp` sub-line (:516) or the signature line
 * (:559-565), draws the h2 upright where this one is italic/300, and stacks
 * at 991 where this band stacks at 780; the two decorative rings are lost
 * too. Every word here is a template literal today, so nothing an editor can
 * change is given up by keeping it in code — the zero-loss option while the
 * owner is not present to give up the two elements. A later round can
 * revisit with the owner.
 *
 * ── D1: a route-scoped band reads its own page ────────────────────────────
 * The avatar is the Images-tab slot `drPortrait` (shared with the doctor
 * band), edited in wp-admin under Pages -> Home -> Images. A code band
 * receives props only (CodeSectionBlock.astro:607-611), so freezing the
 * attachment in the BANDS entry would make a `live` slot dead. This component
 * therefore calls `getPageContent(Astro.url.pathname)` itself — the read the
 * template runs at index.astro:54 — guarded by the `route` prop: on any other
 * route it renders NOTHING and warns, because the slot it asks for exists only
 * on the home page entry. Decision D1, 2026-09-08 (TrustStrip.astro,
 * HomeTechnologyBand.astro and HomeDoctorBand.astro are the earlier instances
 * of the pattern).
 *
 * ── What is live and what is literal ──────────────────────────────────────
 * Live: image("drPortrait") url/width/height/alt (index.astro:560), with the
 * template's own alt fallback "Dr. Bryce Richardson" kept verbatim. Literal:
 * everything else — the eyebrow (:514), the h2 with its `<br>` and
 * `<em class="vs-italic-word">` (:515), the `.pcp` line (:516), the paragraph
 * (:517-520), the three steps (:525-555) and the signature name and role
 * (:561-562) — template literals, frozen here exactly as they were literal in
 * the template. No Section-copy row exists for this band (the page map's
 * copySourceToday: "ALL template literal — no sections row").
 *
 * ── Markup ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Verbatim from index.astro:511-567: `section.process` > `.process-inner` >
 * `.process-head[data-vs-reveal-batch]` (span.eyebrow, h2, span.pcp, p) +
 * `.process-card[data-vs-reveal]` > `.process-steps[data-vs-reveal-batch]` >
 * three `.pstep` (`.num`, span.tagline, h3, p, span.lbl) +
 * `.process-sign[data-vs-reveal]` (`.av[aria-hidden]` > <Image drPortrait>,
 * then a bare <div> of <b> + <small>). The template's blank lines (:522, :557,
 * :558) and the multi-line <p> text nodes are kept at the same indentation,
 * so compressHTML collapses the same runs it collapses today. The only
 * expression in the band is the <Image>, and it sits flush inside `.av` with
 * no text node beside it — exactly as in the template. The `&amp;` at :527
 * is kept as the entity.
 *
 * ── CSS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * home.css:337-422 (the band), the charcoal inversions at :903-911 and the
 * 780px rules at :960-963 (the work order cites :947-950 for these; the
 * sheet's 780 block starts at :934 and the four process lines sit at :960-963
 * today — the values are the ones the page map names: 80px, steps 1fr, pstep
 * bottom hairlines). Astro scopes by attribute, so a bare `.pstep` would tie
 * the page sheet's `.home .pstep` at (0,2,0) and leave bundle order to decide
 * (CodeSectionBlock.astro:437-439); everything below is rooted at `.process`,
 * and the section rule itself is written `section.process` so it outranks
 * `.home .process` rather than tying it. MEASURED with @astrojs/compiler
 * 3.0.1 under the strategy astro 6.1.9 defaults to (`scopedStyleStrategy:
 * "attribute"`, node_modules/astro/dist/core/config/schemas/base.js): the
 * attribute is spliced into EVERY compound, so `section.process` compiles to
 * `section[data-astro-cid-…].process` (0,2,1) and `.process .process-head
 * .eyebrow` to three class+attribute compounds (0,6,0) — above the page
 * sheet's deepest rule, the four-class inversion at :903 (0,4,0). The
 * inversion rules below are rooted `section.process …` anyway ((0,6,1)), so
 * they stay ahead even if the strategy is ever switched to `where`, where the
 * attribute adds nothing and a three-class restatement would tie :903-911.
 * The page primitives the band's elements sit on — `.eyebrow` (:45-49), h2
 * (:54-59 with the :995 ink override folded in), h3 (:54-57, :60), p (:62),
 * em (:63) — are restated too, so the box is whole without the page sheet.
 *
 * The page sheet's `.home` aliases (home.css:14-38) map 1:1 to `--vs-*`
 * tokens and the token names are used here — with ONE exception: `--shadow`
 * (home.css:30) is a raw value on `.home`, NOT an alias of `--vs-shadow`
 * (tokens.css:40 is a different shadow). `.process-card` uses it, so its
 * value is written out literally below. Same computed values either way.
 *
 * The `<em class="vs-italic-word">` is a literal in this file, not set:html,
 * so it carries the scope attribute and needs no :global. Its global rule
 * (global.css:535-539: italic, sage-soft, weight inherit) stays global.
 */
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import { getPageContent } from "../lib/page-content";

interface Props {
  /**
   * The route this band belongs to ("/"). It reads that page's `drPortrait`
   * image slot, so on any other route it renders nothing and warns.
   */
  route: string;
}

const { route } = Astro.props;

// trailingSlash is 'always' (astro.config.mjs:21); normalise both sides anyway
// so "/about-us" and "/about-us/" name the same page, as page-content.ts does.
const withSlash = (p: string) => (p.endsWith("/") ? p : `${p}/`);
const here = Astro.url.pathname;
const onRoute = withSlash(here) === withSlash(route);

if (!onRoute) {
  console.warn(
    `[blocks] HomeProcessBand is scoped to ${route} and was asked to render on ${here} — it reads that page's drPortrait image slot, so it renders nothing here`,
  );
}

type PageImage = { url: string; width: number; height: number; alt: string };

// index.astro:54 — the same read the template runs, only on this route.
let portrait: PageImage | null = null;
if (onRoute) {
  const { image } = await getPageContent(here);
  portrait = image("drPortrait");
}
---

{
  onRoute && portrait && (
    <section class="process">
      <div class="process-inner">
        <div class="process-head" data-vs-reveal-batch>
          <span class="eyebrow">The Vivid Smile Cosmetic Process</span>
          <h2>A smile you imagine should<br><em class="vs-italic-word">feel inevitable, not improvised.</em></h2>
          <span class="pcp">Our proprietary three-step method</span>
          <p>
            Every cosmetic case at Vivid Smiles moves through the same disciplined framework,
            so the final result feels effortless, precise, and unmistakably yours.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="process-card" data-vs-reveal>
          <div class="process-steps" data-vs-reveal-batch>
            <div class="pstep">
              <div class="num">01</div>
              <span class="tagline">Listen &amp; envision.</span>
              <h3>Discovery</h3>
              <p>
                A relaxed, unhurried conversation about what you'd change — and what you'd keep.
                We study your face, your bite, and the way you speak and smile, then translate it
                into a clear design direction.
              </p>
              <span class="lbl">Step One</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pstep">
              <div class="num">02</div>
              <span class="tagline">Preview before we prep.</span>
              <h3>Design</h3>
              <p>
                Using Digital Smile Design and hand-sculpted mock-ups, we render your exact result
                before a tooth is ever touched. You refine it with us, chairside, until it's right.
              </p>
              <span class="lbl">Step Two</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pstep">
              <div class="num">03</div>
              <span class="tagline">Crafted, then delivered.</span>
              <h3>Deliver</h3>
              <p>
                Minimal- or no-prep veneers are shaped to the approved design and bonded with
                heirloom-grade precision. The reveal is the easy part — everything before it is the craft.
              </p>
              <span class="lbl">Step Three</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="process-sign" data-vs-reveal>
          <div class="av" aria-hidden="true"><Image src={portrait.url} width={portrait.width} height={portrait.height} alt={portrait.alt || "Dr. Bryce Richardson"} /></div>
          <div>
            <b>Dr. Bryce Richardson</b>
            <small>Creator · Vivid Smile Cosmetic Process</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  )
}

<style>
  /* ── Page primitives the band sits on (home.css:45-65, :995) ─────────── */
  /* home.css:45-49 */
  .process .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-body);
    font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .28em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--vs-sage); font-weight: 500;
  }
  /* home.css:54-57 + :59, with the :995 h2 → ink override folded in. */
  .process h2 {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-weight: 400; color: var(--vs-ink);
    margin: 0; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 60px);
  }
  /* home.css:54-57 + :60 */
  .process h3 {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-weight: 500; color: var(--vs-sage);
    margin: 0; line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.2vw, 26px);
  }
  /* home.css:62 */
  .process p { margin: 0; color: var(--vs-ink-soft); }
  /* home.css:63 — the <em> is a literal here, so it is scoped like any other element. */
  .process em { font-style: italic; color: var(--vs-sage-soft); font-weight: 300; }

  /* ── The band (home.css:337-422) ─────────────────────────────────────── */
  /* home.css:337-340. `section.process` rather than `.process` so the scoped
     rule is (0,2,1) against the page sheet's `.home .process` (0,2,0) — a
     win, not a tie. Values are the same either way. */
  section.process {
    background: var(--vs-charcoal-green);
    padding: 130px 0; position: relative; overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* home.css:341-348 — the two decorative rings. */
  section.process::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -150px; top: -150px;
    width: 460px; height: 460px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .12); border-radius: 50%;
  }
  section.process::after {
    content: ""; position: absolute; right: -120px; bottom: -120px;
    width: 380px; height: 380px; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, .08); border-radius: 50%;
  }
  /* home.css:349 */
  .process .process-inner { position: relative; max-width: 1180px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 40px; }
  /* home.css:350-365 */
  .process .process-head { text-align: center; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto 56px; }
  .process .process-head .eyebrow { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; }
  .process .process-head .eyebrow::before, .process .process-head .eyebrow::after {
    content: ""; width: 28px; height: 1px; background: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  .process .process-head h2 {
    margin: 22px 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    color: var(--vs-sage);
  }
  .process .process-head .pcp {
    display: block; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; color: var(--vs-ink);
    font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .38em; text-transform: uppercase;
    margin: 18px 0;
  }
  .process .process-head p { font-size: 17px; max-width: 60ch; margin: 0 auto; }

  /* home.css:367-372. `--shadow` is home.css:30's raw value, not a token —
     written out so the plate keeps its shadow without the `.home` block. */
  .process .process-card {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--vs-line);
    border-radius: var(--vs-r-xl);
    padding: 14px;
    box-shadow: 0 24px 60px -30px rgba(40, 40, 30, 0.25), 0 8px 20px -10px rgba(40, 40, 30, 0.08);
  }
  /* home.css:374-379 */
  .process .process-steps {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border-radius: calc(var(--vs-r-xl) - 14px);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* home.css:380-409 */
  .process .pstep {
    padding: 38px 34px 36px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--vs-line);
    position: relative;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;
    background: #fff;
    transition: background .3s ease;
  }
  .process .pstep:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .process .pstep:hover { background: var(--vs-cream); }
  .process .pstep .num {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 56px; color: var(--vs-sage-soft); line-height: .9;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .process .pstep h3 {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-weight: 500; font-size: 22px;
    color: var(--vs-ink); letter-spacing: -0.005em;
  }
  .process .pstep .tagline {
    font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-style: italic; font-weight: 300;
    font-size: 18px; color: var(--vs-sage); line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .process .pstep p { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--vs-ink-soft); }
  .process .pstep .lbl {
    font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .24em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--vs-muted); margin-top: auto;
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; padding-top: 16px;
  }
  .process .pstep .lbl::before { content: ""; width: 18px; height: 1px; background: var(--vs-sage); }

  /* home.css:411-422 */
  .process .process-sign {
    margin-top: 44px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 18px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .process .process-sign .av {
    width: 54px; height: 54px; border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid var(--vs-line); overflow: hidden;
    background: #eee;
  }
  .process .process-sign .av img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; display: block; }
  .process .process-sign b { font-family: var(--vs-font-display); font-weight: 500; color: var(--vs-ink); font-size: 16px; }
  .process .process-sign small { display: block; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .18em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--vs-muted); margin-top: 4px; }

  /* home.css:903-911 — head + sign on charcoal; the white plate interior is
     unchanged. Rooted `section.process` because the page sheet writes these
     four classes deep ((0,4,0)); a three-class restatement plus the scope
     attribute would tie, and `section` breaks the tie in this file's favour. */
  section.process .process-head .eyebrow { color: var(--vs-eyebrow-on-sage); }
  section.process .process-head .eyebrow::before,
  section.process .process-head .eyebrow::after { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, .6); }
  section.process .process-head h2 { color: #fff; }
  section.process .process-head h2 em { color: var(--vs-eyebrow-on-sage); }
  section.process .process-head .pcp { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .85); }
  section.process .process-head p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .85); }
  section.process .process-sign b { color: #fff; }
  section.process .process-sign small { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, .65); }

  /* home.css:934-989 — the 780 block: :960-963. */
  @media (max-width: 780px) {
    section.process { padding: 80px 0; }
    .process .process-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .process .pstep { border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--vs-line); }
    .process .pstep:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
  }
</style>
